{
    "word": "parge",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "7a69435f-3cc1-3bf1-bfc9-a4d9b807b5c4",
                "word": "parge",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e56b63c7-6042-4473-ae14-56606928c31d",
                        "entry_id": "7a69435f-3cc1-3bf1-bfc9-a4d9b807b5c4",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "parges"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ca1e373c-9e11-3969-84d4-6eeebd2918e1",
                        "entry_id": "7a69435f-3cc1-3bf1-bfc9-a4d9b807b5c4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A coat of cement mortar on the face of rough masonry, the earth side of foundation and basement walls."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "608c9136-d53d-4045-aca1-32ba32d5c776",
                                "sense_id": "ca1e373c-9e11-3969-84d4-6eeebd2918e1",
                                "text": "I watch as the mason at the Gilbert house picks up a glob of parge coat on his trowel. He smooths it on, moving from the bottom of the wall to the top. Next, he drapes a white fiberglass mesh from the top of the wall to the bottom and pushes it into the parge coat with his trowel."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "28bf3ce1-b0a7-4031-a954-b32c73efa491",
                                "sense_id": "ca1e373c-9e11-3969-84d4-6eeebd2918e1",
                                "text": "Parging is a single layer of mortar applied directly to the wall with a trowel so that it covers the entire surface. Parges generally are rough and cover the whole masonry surface, but at times they are only applied to the joints or recessed portions of the stonework. Parges might subsequently be whitewashed for a more refined appearance, or used later as the scratch coat for stucco."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2220ce6-6318-4446-803a-1fe5167b70ee",
                                "sense_id": "ca1e373c-9e11-3969-84d4-6eeebd2918e1",
                                "text": "A better method for dealing with efflorescence on masonry is to coat the offending surface with a parge coat of plaster. This is a plaster material that is slightly softer and more porous than the masonry. As the moisture flows through the masonry, it continues through the parge coat and evaporates from the surface, but the salts remain behind in the parge coat."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": [
                    {
                        "linkage_id": "346740c1-2c54-47ea-bb9f-e7dc94f52caf",
                        "source_entry_id": "7a69435f-3cc1-3bf1-bfc9-a4d9b807b5c4",
                        "source_sense_ids": [
                            "ca1e373c-9e11-3969-84d4-6eeebd2918e1"
                        ],
                        "linkage_type": "synonyms",
                        "word": "parging"
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "e18007e0-1d4a-37b6-abb8-f34704ff148c",
                "word": "parge",
                "pos": "verb",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "db7295c0-a1f8-4853-bef9-2b4eb010371a",
                        "entry_id": "e18007e0-1d4a-37b6-abb8-f34704ff148c",
                        "tags": [
